  "description": "Use of ground floor and mezzanine levels to rear as residential (Class C3) use; deconversion of ground floor and mezzanine levels to rear together with two studio flats and one one-bedroom flat to form one three-bedroom maisonette; creation of reconfigured office unit in basement; replacement of all but one window with slimline timber double glazed units installation of secondary glazing to one window; renovation of shopfront; reinstatement of glazed fanlight with opening vent, new solid panel door, and awning; new glazed doors to south elevation of mezzanine garden room; new metal balustrading across rear boundary and raised terrace surface level with walk-on roof lights; replacement of concrete roof tiles with slate and new glazed roof light/ roof access; creation of green roof above mezzanine garden room; removal of modern partition walls and reinstatement of historical plan form as far as possible; reinstatement of historic period features all in connection with the use of building as office at part basement level with the remainder of the building being used as a single residential unit (Class C3) and associated internal alterations. (Linked to 25/09342/FULL)"
